    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining the current JPM position at ~$181.82. The stock sits exactly on the 50-day SMA ($181.82 vs. $181.77) at a genuine technical inflection point. The long-term trend is bullish (16.6% above the rising 200-day SMA, higher low at $179.86 vs. April low of $171.87), but near-term momentum is decelerating (MACD histogram contracted 66% in four days, RSI at 49.72 below midline, four consecutive down sessions, drying volume at 0.867 relative volume). Both analysts agree macro data is unavailable in this historical run, so that cancels out. The fundamental debate is largely a wash. Neither the bull's BUY (requires assumption the 50 SMA holds) nor the bear's SELL (requires assumption the 50 SMA breaks) has a decisive edge. The balanced evidence supports HOLD with clear decision triggers: reduce 25-50% if JPM breaks below $181.77 on above-average volume (next support $171.87, -5.5% downside), and add if it reclaims and holds above $184.66 with expanding volume and re-accelerating MACD.\n\n**Entry Price**: 181.82\n\n**Stop Loss**: 171.87\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-slightly-underweight allocation relative to benchmark; do not deploy new capital until a trigger resolves.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
